/* ---------- Liberia places: the REAL place database ----------
   Generated from ~/workspace/jackwork/data/liberia_places.json
   (14,064 source records; build notes in liberia_places_notes.md
   beside it) plus ~/workspace/jackwork/data/liberia_communities_v2.json
   (183 community records; coverage report in communities_v2_report.md
   beside it) plus ~/workspace/jackwork/data/liberia_communities_v3.json
   (113 community records; coverage report in communities_v3_report.md
   beside it). DO NOT hand-edit names here: every name below is a
   real record from the sources, and no name may be added that is
   not in those files.

   Sources:
   - County and district names, and every town (settlement) with
     its coordinates: HDX "Liberia - Settlements" (NIMAC / UNMIL /
     UNDP via OCHA, Dec 2017), joined to the official HDX COD-AB
     administrative boundaries (OCHA ROWCA / UNMIL) for the county
     and district spellings: 15 counties, 136 districts, 13,899
     surveyed settlement points. Same-name points surveyed more
     than once in the same district (363) are one pick here, so
     PLACE_TOWNS holds the 13,536 unique town names.
   - Communities for Greater Monrovia, from "Communities of the
     Greater Monrovia District" (Wikipedia compilation of LISGIS
     2014 estimates and National Elections Commission data):
     165 named communities under 12 towns.
   - Communities outside Greater Monrovia, from
     liberia_communities_v2.json: 183 real records under 20 towns
     in 13 counties, each record naming its own source in that
     file (GeoNames sections of populated places, OpenStreetMap
     suburb/neighbourhood/quarter tags, and published town
     community lists). 74 of the 183 carry coordinates in the
     source file; 109 come from named lists that publish none.
   - Round 3, from liberia_communities_v3.json: 113 more real
     records under 18 towns (NEC electoral district map labels
     georeferenced against known points, the LEC Kakata network
     inspection report, township lists, and town by town digging;
     each record names its own source and strength in that file).
     38 of the 113 carry coordinates in the source file; 75
     publish none. First community level for Bopolu, Foya,
     Bensonville, Careysburg, Virginia, Brewerville, Zorzor,
     Bong Town and Suakoko; Kakata, Zwedru, Ganta and Tubmanburg
     deepened. The v3 file writes five of those towns by their
     common city names; its rows here are keyed to the town's own
     settlement record, using the research pipeline's documented
     equivalences (Foya = Foya City, Virginia = Central Virginia,
     Harbel = Harbel City, Bong Town = Bong mines, Suakoko =
     Suacoco), so the community names are the file's exactly and
     only the join follows the settlement record. Brewerville
     has no surveyed settlement point of its own in the HDX
     data, so its 10 rows sit with no town point, exactly like
     Garwolon and Johnsonville above. Harbel's 2 records join
     the existing Harbel City key, so the 461 records sit under
     41 town keys here (42 towns counted in the source files).
   - A community pick always uses its own town's surveyed
     coordinates for distance, exactly as the Greater Monrovia
     communities already did; no community coordinate is stored
     here and none is invented. Towns with no sourced community
     list keep no community level: the town pick is the whole
     place. Nothing is invented to fill that gap. In total 461
     community records.

   Shape: PLACE_TOWNS rows are [districtIndex, town, lat, lon];
   PLACE_DISTRICTS rows are [countyIndex, district];
   PLACE_COMMUNITIES rows are [county, district, town, community]. */
